  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Among tens of thousands of hills in the southern part of Central Continent, sunlight through cloud lights green forest on the floating peak while tides crash at its foot.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later scene openings still open on the same pairing: “Central Continent, Fei He mountain.”",
      "chapters": [
        697
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mountain floats on a sea of cloud, grand and piercing the skies.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later text shows Fei He mountain floating among clouds, with trees and ten thousand cranes giving it the living feel of an Immortal’s residence.",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Another stretch names it a floating mountain with clouds, fog, pine forests, and flying cranes.",
      "chapters": [
        827
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its crane flocks are part of the place. Named kinds on the mountain include ironbeak flying crane, fire pellet crane, tailwind crane, cloud mist crane, and stellar light crane, and the Gu Masters on the mountain are famous throughout the world. Immortal Crane Sect uses that territorial advantage: the mountain holds tens of thousands of flying cranes for its people to command.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This is Immortal Crane Sect, named in the same chapter as one of the top ten sects in Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-of-immortal-crane-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang later invites Fang Yuan to look at Fei He mountain, and the narration states outright that it is the base of Immortal Crane Sect.",
      "chapters": [
        858
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-of-immortal-crane-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_he_feng_yang",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan, analyzing Immortal Crane Sect’s pressure, names it as one of the ten great ancient sects of Central Continent, and as having stood at Fei He mountain for hundreds of thousands of years.",
      "chapters": [
        658
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-of-immortal-crane-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Disciples train crane groups on the mountain itself. Fang Zheng practices formations with thousands of iron beak flying cranes on a cliff of Fei He mountain before flying back into Immortal Crane Sect grounds.",
      "chapters": [
        656
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-of-immortal-crane-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sect’s sparring arena is also on the mountain: Fang Zheng’s examination fight against Sun Yuan Hua opens there before crane groups are called from the flocks.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seat-of-immortal-crane-sect",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_sun_yuan_hua"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Shang Qing pavilion stands at the top of the mountain and serves as a grim meeting place for Immortal Crane Sect’s supreme elders.",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_qing_pavilion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Gu Immortal meeting later opens on Fei He mountain and gathers in the hall of affairs at the highest point, where the sect’s first supreme elder chairs discussion among the Immortals present.",
      "chapters": [
        697
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fu Hu blessed land sits with Immortal Crane Sect on this seat. He Feng Yang returns to Fei He mountain and enters Fu Hu blessed land without stopping; anger will then flies from that blessed land to a conference hall at the mountain peak, where wills of the first, second, and third supreme elders remain on watch.",
      "chapters": [
        704
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_fu_hu_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng trains inside that blessed land under sect pressure: one year outside is eight years inside,",
      "chapters": [
        656
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "and the tunnels hold elite rockman guards down to a blood pool deeper in. The current owner of Fu Hu blessed land is the third supreme elder, Lord Tiger Demon, whose rockman slaves are named the best in Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        668
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lord_tiger_demon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang later plants a hole earth Gu sub Gu on Fei He mountain after the Hu Immortal stretch, and Fang Yuan uses Mother Earth belief among fox groups and stonemen higher-ups to move sixty thousand young stonemen into Fei He mountain for sale.",
      "chapters": [
        424
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "supreme-elders-domains-at-the-peak",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_hole_earth_gu",
        "char_fairy_bai_hu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "White Crane Information Tower is a nine-floor Immortal Gu House of Immortal Crane Sect, set in a secluded area on the mountainside of Fei He Mountain amid deep fog and greenery. By that stretch Fang Zheng, as a supreme elder of the sect, still cannot leave Fei He Mountain casually because of his identity.",
      "chapters": [
        1818
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mountainside-gu-house",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_white_crane_information_tower",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    }
  ],
